Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.14,0:00:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Can darkness be a form of light — to say
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.66,0:00:05.22,Default,,0,0,0,,that laws can be undone?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.98,0:00:10.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Can daylight shine within the night, where
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.62,0:00:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,black would color white and sun?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.72,0:00:15.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Are feelings felt?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.94,0:00:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Can they be known?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.36,0:00:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Our minds are always on the move.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.24,0:00:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We say our love is something shown; I ask
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.78,0:00:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,if love can be removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.48,0:00:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Would I fall up if you were down?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.70,0:00:36.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The rules of life are always vague.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.94,0:00:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you sense a soul, like sound?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.24,0:00:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to know if morals fade.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.92,0:00:51.60,Title,,0,0,0,,So shadow-shine, and breath align — but
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.68,0:00:53.66,Default,,0,0,0,,only in my waking mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.22,0:00:59.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought I'd found what was a sign, but I
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.14,0:01:00.82,Title,,0,0,0,,will never draw the lines.
